[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_1]
Satisfaction Survey

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_1_desc]
Good news! According to the latest random sampling survey statistics of the residents of the Empire of Equestria, 94.6% of the residents are “very satisfied” with the rule of Empress Cozy Glow; 3.2% of the residents are “comparatively satisfied” with the rule of Empress Cozy Glow, but in the follow-up survey, they expressed that the actual satisfaction is higher than the option. The remaining 2.2% of the respondents were unable to return the questionnaire due to uncontrollable factors such as injury or inability to go to the polling station.
To address the very few dissatisfied opinions in the survey, the Ministry of Order has sent a special working group to listen to the residents one by one for improvement opinions. The working group will help them improve their living environment and arrange employment. In response to several livelihood issues strongly reflected by local agencies, such as the shortage of prison and hospital capacity, the Ministry of Order will focus on prison expansion and increasing labor reform projects in the next few months. The Ministry of Order is also planning to establish a new collective treatment center for mental illnesses.

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_1_o0]
Good!

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_2]
A Broadcaster’s Encounter

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_2_desc]
“This afternoon, the mighty Friendship Empress Cozy Glow squashed yet another group of rebels who tried to overthrow the great Friendship regime. The rebels...”
A radio pony was broadcasting the news. Before the war, he was just a typesetter, but as his colleagues disappeared one by one, he was surprised to find himself becoming the host of the radio station. Even though he didn’t want to read these obviously artificial news, who would refuse those shiny gold coins? Between a “free” proletarian who could not support himself and a unfree middle class who had status, he would rather be the latter.
“Shut up!” A voice interrupted his broadcast, or recording. The door behind him opened, and a uniformed officer walked in.
“Commissar Grimmler, you look...” He stood up and bowed with a smile.
“There was no rebellion today. You are under arrest. I hope you can learn how to tell the truth in prison.” The officer waved his hoof, and the poor broadcaster was dragged out, his pleading voice disappeared soon.
“Is there any broadcaster left? Hmm, I guess no, then stop broadcasting. The Empress doesn’t like these.” The officer ordered his subordinates as such.

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_2_o0]
Know he knows that silence is golden

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_3]
A Salespony’s Encounter

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_3_desc]
“The Hearth’s Warming Eve is here once again~~”
The salespony Dust Dash is sweeping the floor while humming the song. Even though the floor is shining, she is still repeating the song for the 12th time, and she thinks she should hum it for 25 more times - because the Hearth’s Warming Eve is coming. Even though the atmosphere of this holiday is fading and there is no decent tradition, everypony should still cheer for friendship. However... however today makes D.D. a little disappointed. From the morning to the afternoon, barely anypony came to the store. Or, to say, barely anypony came since the war. Even if they came, they were in a hurry, threw some bits and ran away. But today it still confuses her, “It shouldn’t be like this, it really shouldn’t. Ponies who came here before didn’t act like this.” She sighed, shook her head and looked at the calendar in front of her, an old one she bought before the war.
“Ding-” The bell on the door rang. “Welcome to the Hearth’s Warming General Store, you... you...” D.D. turned around happily, but she was stunned.
“Alright, miss. It seems you are too happy. Please explain it to me.” The leader of a group of ponies, a black stallion, bent down. His cloak covered him completely, and his shadow covered D.D., not even a bit of light could reach her.
“Because... the holiday... is coming?” D.D. shrank to the side fearfully, not daring to face him.
Hearing this, the black stallion immediately looked around the decorations in the store, and his eyes stopped at the old calendar.
“Hmm, the holiday... miss, it seems you have to take a look at the new calendar with me, and learn some new songs. Get up! Miss, you can walk by yourself.” He turned around and looked at the empty square outside.
When she walked out of the door and entered the police car, she saw her best friend. But her best friend avoided her gaze in a hurry, as if she didn’t know her at all. The last few words she heard from her friend were murmured.
“The holiday? She is really losing her mind.”

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_3_o0]
Remember to update your calendar before your funeral

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_4]
A Patient’s Encounter

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_4_desc]
One somehow gloomy day, Lily once again stepped into the old mental counseling center, only to find a fresh face waiting for her.
“Good day, my lady. I’m assuming you are Lily, right?” The new doctor, with a gentle smile, addressed Lily.
Lily looked around and saw the doctor’s picture on the wall, with the caption: “Dr.Schadenpferd, Psychologist, Employee of the Month”.
“Well, it is totally reasonable to feel nervous meeting new doctors. But don’t worry, we are here to help you.” Dr.Schadenpferd seemed to have no intention of explaning what happened to Lily’s previous doctor and continued. But Lily could guess now that it was probably because of the previous doctor’s poor KPI, and maybe Lily herself is partly to blame.
“As you may have heard, the Ministry of Friendship is collaborating on this matter and proposing a new treatment for the mentally troubled. We are here to help you, Lily, to become a better pony.”
The doctor then presented Lily with a contraption called the Joyful Facilitator, a device resembling a harmless medical apparatus. Dr.Schadenpferd assured her that it would enhance her smile and bring her everlasting happiness.
With a mix of curiosity and confusion, Lily consented to the doctors’ proposal. As the Joyful Facilitator hummed to life, Lily felt her face contort into an exaggerated grin, her eyes reflecting a hint of discomfort. Tears welled up, threatening to spill over, but she valiantly held them back.
Dr. Schadenpferd patted Lily’s hoof, exuding a sense of faux empathy. “There, there, dear Lily. Remember, smiling brings joy to all aspects of life. Soon, it will become second nature to you.”
“Pain is just temporary, my dear. Soon, you will be able to smile forever. Please do remember to come every week. Oh... and leave your address, emm... here. Next!”

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_4_o0]
Smile, my dear

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_5]
A Pair of Partners’ Encounter

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_5_desc]
Golden Hoof, a nervous unicorn, raced alongside his companion, Swift Feather, a vigilant pegasus. They weaved through dark alleys, hearts racing.
“Swift Feather, did you see that?” Golden Hoof gasped, his voice trembling. “That pony with the suspiciously large bag? He’s hiding something.”
Swift Feather glanced, her wings tense. “You’re right, Golden Hoof. Let’s report him. But first, let’s make sure we’re not being followed.”
They sought shelter in a decrepit building. Through its broken windows, Swift Feather watched the pony they trailed: his bag slung over his back and he glanced around nervously.
But Golden Hoof wasn’t looking out the window. He was staring at Swift Feather... “Swift Feather, I know we agreed that it’s your turn... but I’ve been having some financial difficulties lately, and I was the one who spotted him, so would you mind if I got the reward this time? Just this once. Next time, I promise it’ll be yours.”
Swift Feather’s wings stopped twitching, and her face darkened. This wasn’t the first time Golden Hoof had done this. Or the second. It was the third time. Swift Feather hadn’t paid her rent this month, and her landlord had been pestering her about it, but she knew she was no match for Golden Hoof’s silver tongue, so she had to swallow her pride and let him have his way again and again.
But this time, Swift Feather decided to act differently. “Oh for the love of Celestia, I’m sick of arguing with you. Golden Hoof, you know as well as I do that it’s the first pony to report who gets the reward, not the first pony to spot. I’m a pegasus, I can fly faster than you can run, so I can get there first. That’s the rule.”
With that, Swift Feather flew out, heading straight for the reporting station, leaving the poor Golden Hoof behind.
Their partnership ended that day, and Golden Hoof never spoke to Swift Feather again. A week later, Swift Feather received an envelope with a check. It read, “Reward: Reporting a pony with a suspiciously large bag.”
She paid her rent, and had some money left over. She thought of Golden Hoof, and felt a little guilty, so she decided to send him the rest of the money, along with an apology letter.
Golden Hoof had the most difficult month without the reward. His financial situation remained dire until he received the letter next month, with a check attached that read, “Reward: Reporting a pony who says ‘Oh for the love of Celestia’.”

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_5_o0]
The landlord was happy, though

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_6]
Equestria Empire Conscription Notice

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_6_desc]
Attention, loyal subjects of the Equestria Empire!
Join the ranks of the glorious Equestrian Armed Forces and experience the thrill of conscription under the wise and benevolent rule of Empress Cozy Glow! In our Empire, we believe that everypony has a duty to lend their hoof to the cause of eternal friendship and harmony, or else.
Enlist now and enjoy a life of adventure, camaraderie, and mandatory friendship lessons! Our conscription program offers exclusive benefits, including:
- Immerse yourself in the splendor of distant and exotic battlefronts! Witness the breathtaking sights of war-torn landscapes and engage in thrilling encounters with various adversaries!
- The opportunity to fight for the greater good of the Empire, with the promise of “protecting harmony”, or something else!
- Forge lifelong bonds with fellow soldiers, as you share your food, shelter, and other resources vital to your survival!
- Experience the pride of wielding traditional equipment, steeped in history and legacy! Revel in the challenges of mastering weaponry that possesses a rich history and unique personality!
- Marvel at the resourceful ingenuity of our logistics teams, as they ensure that every soldier receives precisely the right amount of ammunition and supplies required for their endeavors, never more, probably never less!
- Delve into the art of political subtleties, as our government deploys you to foreign lands with utmost discretion and minimal explanation!
Remember, conscription is not just a duty; it’s an adventure! Join the Equestrian Armed Forces today and help Empress Cozy Glow forge a brighter, friendlier future for all of Equestria. Together, we shall ensure that harmony reigns supreme, and everypony knows their place. Friendship is mandatory, but remember, it’s all for your own good!
(Health insurance not included. All rights reserved by the Equestria Empire Ministry of Defence.)

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_6_o0]
Hooray!... I guess?

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_7]
EEA Introduces New Amendment to Guidebook & Regulations

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_7_desc]
The Equestria Education Association (EEA) has unveiled a brand new amendment to their guidebook and regulations, which hasn’t been updated since the reign of Celestia.
This amendment, ordered by the illustrious Empress Cozy Glow and composed by Chancellor Neighsay, seeks to bring a sense of solemnity and reverence to the education system.
The amendment emphasizes the importance of honoring Empress Cozy Glow in every classroom activity. From the mandatory recitation of her glorious achievements to the compulsory inclusion of her charming portrait in every textbook, the EEA is sparing no effort in ensuring that Cozy Glow’s greatness is etched into the minds of every young pony.
Furthermore, the amendment is also stricter than ever, it’s sternness rivals that of a drill sergeant with a headache. It introduces a plethora of new regulations, ensuring that any hint of non-harmonic thought is swiftly squashed like a bug under a hoof.
While the EEA insists that this amendment is merely meant to foster a sense of unity and devotion to the Empire, speculations are, that Chancellor Neighsay is using this amendment as a greasy pole to climb up the political ladder. Shortly after the announcement of the amendment, Chancellor Neighsay was promoted to the position of Grand Chancellor —— a position newly created by Empress Cozy Glow.
Only time will tell how this amendment will shape the future of Equestria’s education system. Will it be a shining beacon of enlightenment or a dark cloud of conformity? One thing is for sure: the Empire expects every pony to do their duty and honor Empress Cozy Glow, whether they like it or not.

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_7_o0]
Who wrote the last two paragraphs of this article?

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_7_o1]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_8]
Grand Chancellor Neighsay Leads Reform

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_8_desc]
Recently, Grand Chancellor Neighsay announced a new reform plan at a grand ceremony, which will make a radical adjustment to the status and organizational structure of the EEA The Grand Chancellor, renowned for his unwavering dedication to tradition, somehow has taken it upon himself to lead a novel reform, aiming to usher in a new era of enlightenment and intellectualism.
After pledging his unwavering loyalty to the Empress, the Grand Chancellor began his speech with a brief history of the EEA and its role in the development of Equestria. He then went on to explain the necessity of reform, praising the Empress for her foresight and wisdom in recognizing the need for change. He also expressed his gratitude to the Empress for her trust in him, and promised to do his best to fulfill her expectations.
The Empress Cozy Glow responded with a speech of her own, in which she expressed her confidence in the Grand Chancellor and her belief that the reform will be a success. She addressed that she trusts the Grand Chancellor alone to be fully authorized to make all decisions regarding the reform, and that all members of the EEA should cooperate with him to ensure the reform’s success.

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_8_o0]
Cheers!

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_8_o1]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_9]
Minister of Education Neighsay Leads Reform

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_9_desc]
Recently, Grand Chancellor Neighsay announced a new reform plan at a grand ceremony, which will make a radical adjustment to the status and organizational structure of the EEA The Grand Chancellor, renowned for his unwavering dedication to tradition, somehow has taken it upon himself to lead a novel reform, aiming to usher in a new era of enlightenment and intellectualism.
After pledging his unwavering loyalty to the Empress, the Grand Chancellor began his speech with a brief history of the EEA and its role in the development of Equestria. He then went on to explain the necessity of reform, praising the Empress for her foresight and wisdom in recognizing the need for change. He also expressed his gratitude to the Empress for her trust in him, and promised to do his best to fulfill her expectations.
The Empress Cozy Glow responded with a speech of her own, in which she expressed her confidence in the Grand Chancellor and her belief that the reform will be a success. To ensure the success of the reform, the Empress announced that the Grand Chancellor will serve as the Minister of Education of the Equestria Empire during the reform, and the EEA will be placed fully under the administration of the Equestria Empire Ministry of Education.

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_9_o0]
Cheers!

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_9_o1]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_10]
A Worker Pony’s Encounter

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_10_desc]
Today is Glitter Glow’s fifth day of work.
He used to be just a construction worker, but he always believed that he deserved a better job - because his cutie mark was a handsome police hat.
Two months ago, with the completion of the screw production workshop that G.G. and his colleagues had been building, the Equestria Empire Ministry of Industry had no other plans to build new factories in the region this year, so he and his fellow workers lost their jobs. G.G., just to try, sent a special application form to the Equestria Empire Ministry of Order. He even wrote down about his credit of reporting two lazy workers on the construction site.

Now, G.G. has been a security guard in this newly completed screw production workshop for five days. Although his salary barely enough to make ends meet, it is directly from the Equestria Empire Ministry of Order, and for that, nothing can ruin G.G.’s good mood for a day... Well... Maybe there is.
In these five days, he has been consistently seeing the same figure at the factory gate. A dirty vagrant pony, exuding the stench of another pony’s disgust and full of fleas. He was wrapped in a dirty black blanket and has been sleeping here. Why would other ponies tolerate him and let him stay here?
Yesterday afternoon, G.G. was reprimanded by the workshop supervisor because of this. The supervisor said that this pony had been wandering around the factory gate for more than a month and slept at the factory gate every day. Today, G.G. finally erupted, he rushed to the vagrant pony, rudely pulled his dirty blanket, and threw it into the trash can. The vagrant pony cursed and kept talking about... what?
“Y’all ungrateful fxxking ponies.”
G.G. didn’t indulge him, and gave him a hoof in the face. At this time, through the tightly wrapped blanket, G.G. finally saw the face of the pony, it was Glitzerglanz, his former colleague - Glitzerglanz. He was once the strongest pony on the construction site. The fact that the new screw production workshop was completed on time is largely credited to his hard work. But now - Who knows how Glitzerglanz became like this?
G.G. was stunned, and Glitzerglanz covered his face in pain, picked up the blanket in the trash can and ran away. Where will he go in the future? G.G. quickly gave up the idea of continuing to think about it. These have nothing to do with him. He only cares about whether he can get today’s six silver coins and whether he can get off work early and have a good sleep.

It was another two ordinary days, but these two days, finally, Glitzerglanz was no longer sleeping at the factory gate. But the other colleagues in the factory are very different from usual, they have been whispering.
“Have you heard? Glitzerglanz is dead. His body was found in the canal today.”
“Oh, my Cel... Oh my, that’s really sad. Do you know what happened?”
“A month ago he was also working here, just like us, look, the second line on the east side over there. But he has nothing apart from his strength, he is completely ignorant of operating the machine, so he was fired just after two days of work.”
“Alas, what more can you say? Unfortunately his fate is just bounded by his cutie mark - a cart of bricks.”

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_10_o0]
“Factory gate is clean now, I think we don’t need guards anymore.”

