[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_23]
Operation <=Fortress=>

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_23_desc]
The Empire Ministry of Order announced that a large-scale arrest operation was organized in the forbidden jungle yesterday, which successfully captured the reactionary writer and terrorist A.K. Yearling. This was the largest internal operation conducted by the Ministry of Order since its foundation. The Empire deployed many divisions to close in on the dangerous terrorist. This operation highlights the Empire’s confidence in maintaining stability and peace.
During the press conference, regarding the reporter’s question, “What were the casualties of this arrest operation?”, the Ministry of Order gave the reply - er... Sorry, we need to interject an urgent message.
Breaking New: Equestria Empire Ministry of Order has just uncovered a major changeling intelligence network today and successfully arrested one disguised changeling spy leader, who was posed as a reporter. The Empire Ministry of Order urges the general public to be vigilant against changeling espionage activities and work together to maintain the Empire’s safety and stability.
Alright, continuing with the previous report, this operation highlights the Empire’s confidence in maintaining stability and peace. Now let’s take a detailed look at the background of the terrorist A.K. Yearling...

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_23_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_23_o1]
What’s that to do with us?!

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_24]
Empire condemns the Starlight Rebels

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_24_desc]
Recently, the Starlight Rebels launched a war against Manehattan under the name of “ending the slave trade”, which caused serious concern of the Equestria Empire.
“Though the Empire has revoked the special license of Gladmane Group, and though there is indeed a slave trade in Manehattan, this cannot be a reason for the Starlight Rebels to invade.” said the spokespony of the Empire Ministry of Defence.
Considering the security of the cities in the eastern coastal area of Equestria outside Manehattan, Empress Cozy Glow has signed an order requiring Trixie, Duchess of Ponyville, to lead the army to stabilize the southern cities and stop the further actions of the Starlight Rebels.
Regarding whether the Empire has a plan to directly intervene, the spokespony of the Empire Ministry of Defence said: “The historical issues are complicated, and Manehattan and its surrounding areas have long enjoyed a high degree of autonomy...”

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_24_o0]
It’s time to test Trixie’s loyalty

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_24_o1]
Why us?

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_24_o2]
Adding insult to injury!

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_24_o3]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_24_o4]
Dodging the issue, huh?

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_24_TOOLTIP]
Unlock §Rtimed§! decison in §YIndependence Movement§!: §YSend troops to stabilize Eastern Equestria§!

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_25]
Chained by One Chain

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_25_desc]
§b“In leather-clad offices, here the first resemble the last, as they are equally tired, as the ones behind them.”§!

As the “Empress of Friendship”, Cozy Glow has gained unprecedented amount of power, unprecedented number of servants, unprecedented number of “friends”, and unprecedented “responsibilities”. The ill-gotten throne is easy to breed paranoia, and the subsequent result is the autocracy over every detail.
Just like her crown that is heavier than herself, her power has become the chain that binds her. Just like a lottery winner receiving an insanely high income tax bill, the “gifts” of these powers have completely extinguished the remaining joy in Cozy.
Even if she buries herself in documents all day long, even if she is indifferent enough to approve all criminal cases with a “beheading”, the files on her desk are still increasing, almost drowning her petite body. These documents are like lifebuoys with thorns in front of a drowning person, she struggles all the time, but she holds on tightly and refuses to let go.
Maybe when she stops one day, she might recall that afternoon when the Windigos were hovering, the celebration after the victory, perhaps her last joy. But now, she doesn’t even have time to think about it anymore.

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_25_o0]
§RHere the standard of work, is only exhaustion§!

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_26]
Silence

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_26_desc]
When the search report was finally placed on the Empress’s desk, the entire room fell silent for five long minutes. The sergent who submitted the file stood there dumbfounded, neither daring to report nor to leave, just staring at the Empress in complete silence.
The Empress opened the first page of the report, where the word “Dead” were written in bold red letters. She seemed unsurprised, as the lack of response to her letters for weeks had already hinted at the same outcome.
“Oh... OK... Alright. You go and find out who did this.” The Empress left the office with only this short command, leaving the sergent drenched in sweat.

The investigation began three weeks ago, with the Empress providing no details or reasons, only a single name is provided for the EEMO to investigate... When the sergent in charge of the investigation first looked at the file, he thought it was just another radical protester among the “Imitators” who had crossed the line and was to be made an example of. It was only after going through the files that he realized that things were not as simple as they assumed. When he saw the photo of the pony in question, he felt a chill run down his spine.

After three weeks of investigation, the sergent had visited almost every office in the EEMO and the Canterlot Police Department, questioning every subordinate and officer, before finally piecing together the terrifying truth. And now, what should be done?
“Find out who did this.” This seemingly light command could be the end of us all. But in the face of such a major incident, if we cannot find all those involved, then the scapegoat could be the entire investigation team.

So, the sergent has only one option left —

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_26_o0]
Better kill all than let the guilty escape!

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_27]
A Lighter Hoof

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_27_desc]
After that night ended, the “Imitator Movement” also came to an end. Thousands of associates were imprisoned or fled the empire.
But the ending of the incident is not the end of its aftermath. The “Imitator” has become a hidden culture in the streets and alleys: in those dark corners, the walls are painted with the portrait of the Empress, some are caricatured, and more are just normal images, so that the police have no reason to arrest them. The propaganda machine of the empire has tried countless times to promote the greatness of the Empress, to make the Empress’s portrait, flag, and autobiography appear in every pony’s home and every street. Now, their efforts have become a reality, but in a way they cannot control.

Soon, “printing, painting, or holding the Empress’s portrait” became a new crime, joining the long laws of the Equestria Empire.
Until that day, the Empress, who left the palace, sat in her palanquin and opened the curtain to see an alley in Canterlot City. At the end of the alley, an EEMO police officer was beating a teenager “Imitator” dressed as Cozy Glow.
Empress Cozy Glow ordered the convoy to stop, and she sat there for a long time, until the pony was beaten to death. The accompanying Canterlot Police Chief finally noticed the Empress’s behavior and walked up to her, his voice trembling as he reported: “I’m so sorry, your Majesty! You shouldn’t have seen this! This is our negligence at work. Please believe me, I promise you, we will worker harder! I promise you will never see them again! If we see ‘Cozy Glow’ on the street in the future, we will instantly kill them on sight!”
The police chief realized that he had said the wrong thing, his face turned pale, he felt dizzy, his heart was pounding, his hooves were shaking, his throat was dry, and he wanted to explain but couldn’t say a word.

After a long time, the Empress just reached out her hoof out of the window and patted the chief’s back.
“No, Chief, you go and tell your subordinates, please be more gentle in the future. A lighter hoof, remember.”

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_27_o0]
A lighter hoof, a lighter hoof

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_28]
The Mastermind

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_28_desc]
When the sergent met the Empress again, it had been another four weeks. The investigation team had secretly pieced together a list containing thousands of names, including Canterlot police officers, EEMO grassroots, and even the senior members of the Royal Commission who was directly involved in the “Imitator Movement” square incident that night.
In fact, under the fear of death threats, the investigation team only took more than a week to complete the list. But the sergent heard that the Empress had not been handling government affairs, there were rumors that the Empress was crying every night in the palace, and other rumors that she heard Cozy shouting “Kill them all!”, so he waited until the Empress’s mood improved slightly before daring to report.
At the same time, the news of the investigation had long been leaked, and the true identity of the deceased shocked the entire empire’s political society. The entire Canterlot government was highly nervous, and many mid-level to high-level officials who thought themselves involved had already arranged routes to leave the country.

The Empress, who was walking in the garden, carefully read the list provided by the sergent. The sergent thought he would wait for the Empress’s order to “execute them all immediately”, but he did not expect to receive a question:
“Why didn’t you list the mastermind on the list of so many murderers?”

At that very moment, the sergent felt all his blood frozen. What did our investigation miss? Empress Cozy Glow is aware of the mastermind, but after four to five weeks of investigation, we missed? The sergent started to have flashbacks about his lives, imagining his last minutes of life. It’s the end. We f**ked up. The entire investigation team is done.
Still, the sergent managed to calm himself down and quickly started thinking. Carefully, he asked tentatively, “The mastermind... are you referring to the participants of the ‘Imitator Movement’ and those despicable resistance organizations behind them? Then please rest assured, we will arrange a re-investigation immediately, and we will not let go of any —”

Empress Cozy Glow shook her head and sighed.
“It was me. It was me.”

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_28_o0]
What?

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_29]
Change

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_29_desc]
No pony knows what happened. We only know that the empire is changing.

If you only get political news through reading newspapers, then you probably won’t realize any difference; if you have relatives working in the empire’s government, then maybe... just maybe, you might hear some unreliable rumors.

Anyway, since the “Imitator Movement” evolved into a bloody conflict, a silent terror has tightly wrapped around the entire empire’s government. It is rumored that the Empress was furious and ordered the formation of an investigation team to thoroughly eliminate the traitors in the empire’s government. The investigation team noted down thousands of names in the shadows of Canterlot.

No pony knows the details of the investigation team, no pony knows what the conclusion of the investigation is, and no pony can even confirm the existence of such a mythical investigation team. Day after day, the masses can only glimpse at an iceberg tip of secrets in side the Empire, through the abnormally high resignation and disappearance rates of high-ranking officials — the empire is undergoing a great purge. But this speculation was quickly denied, as the public saw those missing high-ranking officials appearing in Las Pegasus on vacation, or starting trade in the Crystal Empire...

This terror also stopped abruptly. Without reason, without result, without news, without rumors, the terror that shrouded the entire empire just, vanished in an instant, just as it was about to reach its peak.

Even if the mythical investigation team really existed, this group probably disbanded within a day. The empire’s government completely stopped the investigation of the “Imitator Movement”, and many arrested radical protesters were inexplicably released. The EEMO withdrew a large number of police stationed on various streets, and the empire’s government did not issue any statement to explain everything.

No pony knows what happened. We only know that the empire is changing.

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_29_o0]
The Age of Change

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_31]
Escape from the Cage

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_31_desc]
When the army entered the Canterlot Palace, Cozy Glow was no longer in the palace. She did not take the guards with her, nor did she take anything except her crown. Despite the order to search, she disappeared without a trace.

It is said that Cozy Glow escaped from Canterlot City, and the last time she was seen was in a small village near the Everfree Forest. The former Empress is now ragged and unkempt, but even when she sleeps in the bushes, she clings tightly to her crown. The crown was the only thing that made the witnesses not mistake her for an ordinary wandering pony.

At that time, the village had not received the national wanted notice for Cozy Glow. She came to the village to ask for directions, wanting to escape into the Everfree Forest along the road opened up by the caravan. At the entrance of the forest, she was tripped by a vine, and the crown fell to the ground and rolled into the nearby mud pit.
Cozy Glow lay there, not choosing to pick up her crown, but just staring calmly as the crown sank bit by bit into the mud pit. When the crown completely disappeared into the mud pit, Cozy Glow stood up, making a crazy laugh, but it seemed like a sincere laugh, perhaps she finally felt happy again after so many years. The moment she lost her crown was like the moment she got her crown years ago.

After that, Cozy Glow staggered into the Everfree Forest like a deranged pony. Since then, no pony has seen her again.

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_31_o0]
Alas...

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_31_o1]
Alas...

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_32]
New Well

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_32_o0]
Labor is magic!

[en.EVENT_C01_MAIN_32_desc]


